# What an image build must never see.
#
# Two entries here are not about size. `.env` carries a KEK and `.certpilot/`
# holds the development PKI's private keys; every Dockerfile in this tree does
# `COPY . .` in its builder stage, and a build context is handed to the daemon
# whole before any instruction runs. A certificate management product baking its
# own private keys into a layer is the specific failure this file prevents.
.env
.env.*
.certpilot/
config.dev.yaml
*.pem
*.key

# Not inputs to any binary.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
bin/
docs/
brand/
*.md
*.log
.DS_Store

# `deploy/` is deliberately NOT excluded: the frontend image copies
# deploy/docker/nginx.conf out of it. Only the compose files themselves are
# never build inputs, and they cost nothing.
deploy/.env
